**Safe harbour** is the clause that turns good-faith testing into authorised testing. disclose.io, an open project that publishes model policy text, defines it as language that "lets people acting in good faith, as the recipient defines it, report security issues without fear of legal repercussions". Its bug bounty template says research conducted under the policy is considered:

- "Authorized concerning any applicable anti-hacking laws", with a promise not to "initiate or support legal action against you for accidental, good-faith violations";
- authorised under anti-circumvention laws;
- exempt from the terms of service where they would interfere with research;
- "lawful, helpful to the overall security of the Internet, and conducted in good faith".
